BT /F2 10 Tf 54 692 Td (PROBLEM) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 678 Td (Each item has a weight and value. Maximize total value in a capacity-limited bag;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 665 Td (    fractions of items are allowed.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 645 Td (GREEDY CHOICE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 631 Td (Compute value / weight for every item, sort by this ratio descending, then take as much) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 618 Td (    as possible from each item in that order.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 598 Td (PSEUDOCODE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 584 Td (sort items by value/weight descending) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 571 Td (for each item:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 558 Td (    take min\(item weight, remaining capacity\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 545 Td (    add its proportional value) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 525 Td (EXAMPLE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 511 Td (Capacity 50; items \(weight,value\) are \(10,60\), \(20,100\), \(30,120\). Take the first two) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 498 Td (    and 20 of the final item's 30 weight; value = 240.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 478 Td (COMPLEXITY) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 464 Td (Sorting: O\(n log n\); selection scan: O\(n\). Overall time: O\(n log n\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 444 Td (IMPORTANT) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 430 Td (This greedy rule is optimal for fractional knapsack, but not generally for 0/1 knapsack) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 417 Td (    where items cannot be split.) Tj ET
